    "aliases": [],
    "description": "``strict_types`` is an execution directive, that makes PHP more strict when applying the types. In particular, it doesn't cast scalar values automatically, but raise an error. \n\n``strict_types`` is an option per file, and is set with the ``declare()`` function.",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    declare(strict_types=1);\n    \n    function trumpet(int $a) {}\n\n    trumpet(1);\n    trumpet(1.3);\n    //Fatal error: Uncaught TypeError: trumpet(): Argument #1 ($a) must be of type int, float given,\n\n?>",
